{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wu2eljtivxvqhscokdv24hlt5xyaofzm5qpdpv3imochnpwrbpka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. Here's what happened.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a trimmed copy of **stb_ds.h** (dynamic arrays + hash maps + string arena) plus the `strkey`/`str_put` helpers from its test section. The public header declares only `str_put`, but the `.so` exports **16** symbols.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all in the crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — all 16 `nm -D` symbols, mapped to C definition sites; the `static` helpers that correctly stay private; `stbds_unit_tests` (declared but never defined, so exported by neither).\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — **45 rows**, one per distinct rejection/assert/NULL-deref, grepped out of the C.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — **47 rows** = pruned cross-product of `mode` × `table->string.mode` × element shape × count × probe shape × tombstone state × arena shape.\n\n**Feature combinations: exactly one.** `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; `cargo check --no-default-features` and `cargo check` are both clean, 0 warnings.\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed in `src/lib.rs`\n\n1. **All 11 `assert()`s were missing.** `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is unset ⇒ `NDEBUG` undefined ⇒ `__assert_fail` is imported by the C `.so`, so asserts are *live*. Two of them (`assert(slot >= 0)`, `assert(b->index[i] == final_index)` in `hmdel_key`) are **reachable** via a non-zero `keyoffset` — the C aborts while the Rust was writing through `storage[-1]`. Ported as `stbds_assert` → `abort()`.\n2. **Aligned `char**` dereferences.** `elemsize == 1` puts element *i* at `a+i`, so the C does *unaligned* pointer loads/stores; Rust's `*p` panicked. Replaced with `read_unaligned`/`write_unaligned`.\n3. **Overflow-checked arithmetic** (`used_count -= 1`, `length -= 1`, `512 << (block>>1)`, `len << 56`, …) made explicitly `wrapping_*` so debug and release agree with C.\n4. **`ptr::copy`/`write_bytes` → libc `memcpy`/`memmove`/`memset`**, and `ptr::add/sub` → wrapping address arithmetic.\n\n## Phases B/C/D — results\n\n`./run_tests.sh` and `./run_tests.sh --release`: **79 test functions, 0 failures each**, `nm -D` diff **empty** (16/16, no extras, no non-libc undefined symbols).\n\nBoth `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and compared after *every single operation* on: array header, all live element bytes, the whole `stbds_hash_index`, and every `hash[8]`/`index[8]` of every bucket. Crash rows are compared by re-execing the test binary per library and asserting the same signal — against the **release** `.so`, since debug instrumentation turns a NULL deref into SIGABRT instead of SIGSEGV.\n\n**Two things worth flagging:**\n\n- `cargo test` does **not** rebuild a `cdylib`, so my early runs were loading a stale `.so`. `assert_fresh` now hard-fails on that, and `run_tests.sh` builds first.\n- I mutation-tested the harness: **22 injected bugs, 21 caught**. Two initially survived and both were genuine coverage gaps I then closed with new tests (`err_24b` for \"temp_key untouched in the second probe loop\", `cfg_46b` for the multi-bucket rehash spill). The one remaining survivor is provably equivalent — removing only `assert(slot >= 0)` still aborts on the next assert; removing both *is* caught.\n\nSome configurations are documented as **untestable rather than tested**, because the C's own result depends on a heap address (e.g. `hmdel_key` with `mode >= 2` on a pointer-key table hashes the *bytes of a stored pointer*). Those are listed with reasons in `CONFIGS.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":385317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1216,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84845924-0592-4851-88b6-27cefaf022f4","uuid":"f6285e5e-bd36-4fb6-96d1-a603c335a2ec","timestamp":"2026-08-20T17:07:43.573Z"}
